# CRUD Factory codebase

This repo hosts up to **10 customer-facing apps** on **Cloudflare** (Workers, D1, automatic SSL). Tech **varies per app** — pick a stack when scaffolding.

## Layout

- `apps/<slug>/` — deployable apps (one folder per product)
- `packages/database` — Drizzle schema + D1 migrations (shared)
- `packages/auth` — Better Auth (used by `next-d1` stack)
- `templates/<stack>/` — sources for `pnpm new-app`
- `platform/stacks.json` — stack catalog
- `apps.registry.json` — deployed app registry (slug, stack, worker name, D1 name)

## Add an app

```bash
pnpm new-app <slug> --stack next-d1   # or vite-d1, hono-d1
./scripts/provision-cloudflare.sh <slug>
```

Do **not** copy `apps/demo` by hand — use templates via `new-app`.

## Stacks

| Stack | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `next-d1` | Full web app + email/password auth + CRUD UI |
| `vite-d1` | React SPA + Hono API on one Worker |
| `hono-d1` | JSON API only (mobile / separate UI) |

## Conventions

- Each app has its own **D1** database (`crud-<slug>`).
- `APP_ID` env matches registry `slug`.
- Prefer extending `packages/database` for shared tables; app-specific tables only when necessary.
- Deploy per app: `pnpm --filter <slug> deploy`.
